  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\varphi(n) \\text{ is even for } n \\geq 3; \\quad \\varphi(n) = n-1 \\Leftrightarrow n \\text{ prime}; \\quad a \\mid b \\Rightarrow \\varphi(a) \\mid \\varphi(b); \\quad \\varphi(a)\\varphi(b) \\leq \\varphi(ab); \\quad \\varphi(n) = n\\prod_{p|n}(1-1/p); \\quad \\varphi(\\gcd(a,b))\\varphi(ab) = \\varphi(a)\\varphi(b)\\gcd(a,b)",
    "plain": "Structural properties of Euler totient function: parity (even for n>=3), prime characterization (phi(n)=n-1 iff prime), divisibility monotonicity, super-multiplicativity, the product formula, and the GCD-totient identity.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Foundational properties connecting totient to primality, divisibility, and factorization",
      "Product formula underpins sieve methods and average-order estimates",
      "GCD identity unifies multiplicativity and divisibility into one formula"
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "phi(n) even for n>=3",
      "phi(n)=n-1 iff n prime",
      "a|b implies phi(a)|phi(b)",
      "phi(a)*phi(b)<=phi(ab)",
      "Product formula phi(n)=n*prod(1-1/p)",
      "GCD-totient identity"
    ],
